0 more on item 0 alone.\n\nThis puts candidates 0 and 1 (×1.2) at the bottom. Candidate 7 (item 0 at ×1.2) is also poor. Candidates 3 (×1.1) and 6 (×1.1 every 2 days) lose to their ×1.0 counterparts.\n\n**Daily against every 2 days, both at ×1.0 (candidate 2 against candidate 4).**\n- Fewer order days save 13 × 42 = 546.\n- Holding the second day's stock costs about 183 for item 0 and 239 for item 1, about 422 in total.\n- Stock arrives earlier, so there are slightly fewer shortages.\n- Net, candidate 4 comes out about 150–250 ahead of candidate 2.\n\n**Every 3 days at ×1.1 (candidate 5).** It saves about 756 in order fees against daily ordering. But it pays about 935 more in holding, and the ×1.1 surplus costs a further ~500. That puts it roughly level with candidate 3.\n\nCandidate 4's main rival is candidate 2, about 200 behind, and that gap is comparable to the randomness in the outcome. That's why p_best is only about 0.55."}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 4589, "cache_read_input_tokens": 2304, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 4589}, "output_tokens": 5, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "global", "speed": "standard"}, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "timestamp": "2026-10-27T10:08:51.659Z", "request_id": "req_011CgSZCX6xYHius5t9maRKS"}, {"type": "stream_event", "event": {"type": "content_block_stop", "index": 1}, "parent_tool_use_id": null}, {"type": "stream_event", "event": {"type": "content_block_start", "index": 2, "content_block": {"type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_01W9wpKDnNYsifUN6F6FCgqQ", "name": "StructuredOutput", "input": {}, "caller": {"type": "direct"}}}, "parent_tool_use_id": null}, {"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-opus-5-5", "id": "msg_011CgSZCXPaarw11jdoAXXLb", "type": "message", "role"